/* TC002CLI/main.swift — hilfetext */
"cli.hilfe" = "mqtttc002 — send messages to an Ulanzi TC002.\n\nUses the setup of the MQTT-TC002 app: broker, password and clocks are read\nfrom there. Setting up happens in the app only.\n\nUSAGE\n  mqtttc002 [send] <text>          send text to the clocks\n  mqtttc002 delete <display>       remove a named display\n  mqtttc002 switch <display>       switch to a display\n  mqtttc002 clocks                 list the clocks that are set up\n  mqtttc002 icons                  list the icons that are there\n  mqtttc002 help                   this text\n\nOPTIONS FOR \"send\"\n  --to <clock>        name or address; may be given more than once.\n                      Without it, the selection that applies in the app.\n  --name <display>    name of the display on the clock (default: cli)\n  --color #RRGGBB     default: #00FF66\n  --icon <number>     an 8x8 icon to the left of the text\n  --font <name>       default: Silkscreen\n  --size <number>     default: 8\n  --bold              bold cut, if the font has one\n  --upper             everything in capitals\n  --top|--middle|--bottom       vertical alignment (default: middle)\n  --left|--center|--right       horizontal alignment (default: left)\n  --margin <number>   rows left free at top/bottom (default: 1)\n  --gap <number>      empty columns between the characters (default: 1)\n  --duration <seconds>  how long the clock shows the display\n  --speed langsam|mittel|schnell   only for scrolling text\n  --device-font       use the clock's built-in font instead of\n                      rasterizing here. Knows no umlauts.\n  --dry-run           only show what would be sent\n\nThe German names work as well: senden, loeschen, umschalten, uhren, hilfe,\n--an, --farbe, --schrift, --groesse, --fett, --gross, --oben, --mitte,\n--unten, --links, --zentriert, --rechts, --rand, --abstand, --dauer,\n--tempo, --geraeteschrift, --trocken.\n\nEXAMPLES\n  mqtttc002 \"Coffee ready\"\n  mqtttc002 send \"Mail is here\" --icon 1673 --color \"#FFAA00\"\n  mqtttc002 send Attention --to Kitchen --duration 10 --center\n  mqtttc002 delete cli\n\nTexts that are too long scroll by themselves; the app does the same.";

